{
  "kings2.4.p1.b1": {
    "text": "Your servant, my husband, is dead … And now his creditor is coming to take my two children as his slaves!",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:1"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "kings2.4.p1.b2": {
    "text": "How can I help you? … Tell me, what do you have in the house?",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:2"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "kings2.4.p1.b3": {
    "text": "Your servant has nothing in the house but a jar of oil.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:2"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "kings2.4.p1.b4": {
    "text": "Go … borrow jars, even empty ones, from all your neighbors. Do not gather just a few.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:3"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "kings2.4.p2.b1": {
    "text": "So she left him, and after she had shut the door behind her and her sons, they kept bringing jars to her, and she kept pouring.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:5"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "kings2.4.p2.b2": {
    "text": "Bring me another.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:6"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "kings2.4.p2.b3": {
    "text": "There are no more jars.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:6"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "kings2.4.p2.b4": {
    "text": "Then the oil stopped flowing.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:6"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "kings2.4.p3.b1": {
    "text": "One day Elisha went to Shunem, and a prominent woman who lived there persuaded him to have a meal. So whenever he would pass by, he would stop there to eat.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:8"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "kings2.4.p3.b2": {
    "text": "Behold, now I know that the one who often comes our way is a holy man of God.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:9"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "kings2.4.p3.b3": {
    "text": "Please let us make a small room upstairs and put in it a bed, a table, a chair, and a lamp for him.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:10"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "kings2.4.p4.b1": {
    "text": "Look, you have gone to all this trouble for us. What can we do for you?",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:13"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "kings2.4.p4.b2": {
    "text": "I have a home among my own people",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:13"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "kings2.4.p4.b3": {
    "text": "she has no son … and her husband is old.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:14"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "kings2.4.p4.b4": {
    "text": "At this time next year, you will hold a son in your arms.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:16"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "kings2.4.p4.b5": {
    "text": "No, my lord … Do not lie to your maidservant, O man of God.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:16"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "kings2.4.p5.b1": {
    "text": "My head! My head!",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:19"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "kings2.4.p5.b2": {
    "text": "Carry him to his mother.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:19"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "kings2.4.p5.b3": {
    "text": "… the boy sat on her lap until noon, and then he died.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:20"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "kings2.4.p5.b4": {
    "text": "And she went up and laid him on the bed of the man of God. Then she shut the door and went out.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:21"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "kings2.4.p6.b1": {
    "text": "Why would you go to him today? … It is not a New Moon or a Sabbath.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:23"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "kings2.4.p6.b2": {
    "text": "Everything is all right",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:23"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "kings2.4.p6.b3": {
    "text": "Are you all right? Is your husband all right? Is your child all right?",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:26"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "kings2.4.p6.b4": {
    "text": "Everything is all right.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:26"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "kings2.4.p7.b1": {
    "text": "Leave her alone, for her soul is in deep distress, and the LORD has hidden it from me and has not told me.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:27"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "kings2.4.p7.b2": {
    "text": "Did I ask you for a son, my lord? Didn’t I say, ‘Do not deceive me?’",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:28"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "kings2.4.p7.b3": {
    "text": "As surely as the LORD lives and as you yourself live, I will not leave you.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:30"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "kings2.4.p7.b4": {
    "text": "Gehazi went on ahead of them and laid the staff on the boy’s face, but there was no sound or response.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:31"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "kings2.4.p8.b1": {
    "text": "When Elisha reached the house, there was the boy lying dead on his bed.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:32"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "kings2.4.p8.b2": {
    "text": "So he went in, closed the door behind the two of them, and prayed to the LORD.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:33"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "kings2.4.p8.b3": {
    "text": "… the boy’s body became warm.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:34"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "kings2.4.p8.b4": {
    "text": "… the boy sneezed seven times and opened his eyes.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:35"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "kings2.4.p9.b1": {
    "text": "Call the Shunammite woman.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:36"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "kings2.4.p9.b2": {
    "text": "Pick up your son.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:36"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "kings2.4.p9.b3": {
    "text": "She came in, fell at his feet, and bowed to the ground. Then she picked up her son and went out.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:37"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "kings2.4.p10.b1": {
    "text": "When Elisha returned to Gilgal, there was a famine in the land.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:38"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "kings2.4.p10.b2": {
    "text": "Put on the large pot and boil some stew for the sons of the prophets.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:38"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "kings2.4.p10.b3": {
    "text": "There is death in the pot, O man of God!",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:40"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "kings2.4.p11.b1": {
    "text": "Now a man from Baal-shalishah came to the man of God with a sack of twenty loaves of barley bread from the first ripe grain.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:42"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "kings2.4.p11.b2": {
    "text": "How am I to set twenty loaves before a hundred men?",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:43"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "kings2.4.p11.b3": {
    "text": "Give it to the people to eat … for this is what the LORD says: ‘They will eat and have some left over.’",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:43"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "kings2.4.p11.b4": {
    "text": "So he set it before them, and they ate and had some left over, according to the word of the LORD.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "2 Kings 4:44"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  }
}
